Indeed.

If there's a specific artifact longsword that
you would particularly like to have, it may be
worth wishing for that one first, _then_ doing
a sacrifest to get unrestricted.  Being given
any longsword by your diety will unrestrict
all of them, and artifact longswords are common
enough that an extended sacrifest is very likely
to net you at least one.

But otherwise, as a priest, your artifact weapon
wishing options are mostly Mjollnir and Mjollnir.
If that's not your cup of tea, it's sacrifice time.

Magicbane is not a particularly good option for
a priest.  It's tempting for Monks (because it
helps avoid the need to wear body armor) and a
good option for any role that can get Expert
in dagger, but otherwise meh.

Grayswandir is great for any character, regardless
of alignment.  If I found it on the floor, I'd use 
it even if restricted and chaotic.  However, I don't
think I'd ever spend a wish for a weapon I'm restricted 
in, and the odds of getting unrestricted in saber are 
not so good, as there are only two artifact sabers,
neither of which is chaotic IIRC.

And yeah, the weapon options list is somewhat shorter
for priests than most other roles. 

Slash'em has a larger variety of artifact weapon 
options for chaotic characters, but Slash'em also
has even more ways to die than NetHack, if you can
imagine such a thing, so it's really not a good
variant for beginners.  Wait until you've ascended
several different roles in vanilla before going there.

